content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal leakage of about one drop per second at the shaft seal. The manual lists shaft-seal leakage as a fault symptom with corrective action 'Replace mechanical seal (5.2). Check alignment (5.4).' No acceptable leakage rate is documented, so this cannot be compared with a numeric limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration of 3.4 mm/s is in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation') of Figure 3. It is below the Zone C threshold of 4.5 mm/s ('Restricted - plan maintenance') and well below the Zone D threshold of 7.1 mm/s ('stop the pump'). The manual says to classify the highest reading from both bearing housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature of 70 C is exactly at the upper limit of the normal band (normal up to 70 C). It is below the 80 C alarm and the 90 C trip, so no stop is required, but there is no margin left. The manual's limit is for bearing housing temperature; it is assumed the reported 'housing' reading is the bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall: no reading reaches a stop threshold (Zone D vibration or 90 C trip). The seal leak needs planned seal replacement, and the temperature at the top of the normal band should be watched. This supports a planned job (P2) rather than an immediate stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: worn or cracked seal faces on the component seal HF3-450. The service bulletin reports early field failure of HF3-450 on pumps from serial HF3-22000 because of a revised sleeve tolerance, and this pump (HF3-22871) is in that range.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible: the seal has run dry. Seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge, and the seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible: shaft misalignment. This is listed as a cause of seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature, and may explain vibration in Zone B together with temperature at the normal limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contributing to temperature: over-greasing or bearing wear may be raising bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before starting, confirm the serial plate reads HF3-22871. This is HF3-22000 or above, so service bulletin SB-2026-014 applies: use cartridge seal HF3-450B and do NOT fit HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment (assembly mass 68 kg).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and the impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and sleeve. Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring, and replace it if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, inspect the bearings and impeller, since vibration is in Zone B and temperature is at the normal limit. Replace both bearings as a pair if either shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new cartridge seal HF3-450B. It is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the seal gland nuts (M10) to 30 Nm, as SB-2026-014 requires for HF3-450B. Do NOT use the manual's 25 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the other fasteners to Table 5 (lightly oiled threads): impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, and bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm if disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity in the bearings, because over-greasing is a cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out laser shaft alignment, as required after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing and as recommended for seal leakage. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm, angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from the pump discharge is in place, and make sure the pump is primed so the seal never runs dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Record the bearing housing temperature and compare it with the limits: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever the casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Have one available; fit only if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before dismantling.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly (68 kg).",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the seal dry. Confirm the Plan 11 flush and prime the pump before starting.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump if vibration reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s) or the bearing housing reaches the 90 C trip. Raise an alarm at 80 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the bearings are found worn, add a bearing pair replacement: 6.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. This pump's serial, HF3-22871, is above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies and the torque is 30 Nm. The previous shift's note that '25 Nm is correct for all pumps' is wrong for this asset. 25 Nm applies only to pumps below HF3-22000 that use HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal part: the manual parts list gives component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. Use HF3-450B on this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve check: manual procedure 5.2 says to inspect the sleeve for scoring with no stated limit, and HF3-450 needs sleeve measurement. The bulletin says HF3-450B needs no sleeve measurement and sets a replacement limit of more than 0.1 mm scoring for HF3-455. The bulletin applies to this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "No acceptable seal leakage rate is documented, so one drop per second cannot be compared with a limit.",
    "Was the 3.4 mm/s reading the highest from both bearing housings, and was it measured in mm/s RMS as Figure 3 requires?",
    "Was the 70 C reading taken on the bearing housing, and is it trending upward? No trend data is available.",
    "Which seal is currently fitted (original HF3-450 or a previous replacement), and how long has it been in service?",
    "The evidence does not give a site lockout/tagout procedure, PPE requirements or the drain-down method.",
    "Stock availability and lead time for HF3-450B and HF3-455 are unknown.",
    "The evidence does not state whether the bulletin changes any torques other than the seal gland nut, or the gland nut thread condition; Table 5 values assume lightly oiled threads.",
    "The evidence gives no grease type or correct grease quantity for the bearings."
  ]
}
